{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/159052-funerary-rites","id":159052,"title":"Funerary Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-04T08:07:26-07:00","id":159052,"title":"Funerary Rites","content":"Seeing as how Geist spends a lot of its time covering funerary traditions and rites, I wanted to see if anyone knew of any strange traditions they've come across in their travels? I'll start...<br /> <br /> I'm Irish, and for my brother's funeral, there was a real, old school wake - his body lied in the coffin in our house for 3 days before he was buried, and people came and went throughtout, with a small Catholic...thing (prayers, etc) at the start. Some of the rules involved in this were:<br /> <br /> - The body was never allowed to be in the room alone. Someone had to stay in the room at all times, even through the night, and were not allowed to sleep there.<br /> - No animals allowed in the room (pretty self explanitory, but I could see how you could do something with that in Geist)<br /> - No mirrors allowed in the room - any mirrors there had to be taken down<br /> - No clocks allowed in the room - see the rule about the mirrors.<br /> - One window had to be open at all times<br /> - The door could never be closed<br /> - There had to be rosary beads wrapped around the hands.<br /> <br /> There were other small things here and there, but that was the majority. Anyone else got anything to offer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"}